# Connecting GameObjects

Often you need to access other GameObjects or their components. Two common ways:

1. **Public field** (drag and drop in Inspector):
```csharp
public GameObject player;
public Transform target;
```
2. **Find by name/tag** (less efficient):
```csharp
GameObject player = GameObject.Find("Player");
GameObject enemy = GameObject.FindWithTag("Enemy");
```

Public references are faster and more reliable.

slides.codeSnippet:
using UnityEngine;

public class ChaseTarget : MonoBehaviour
{
    public Transform target;
    public float speed = 5f;

    void Update()
    {
        if (target != null)
        {
            Vector3 direction = (target.position - transform.position).normalized;
            transform.Translate(direction * speed * Time.deltaTime);
        }
    }
}
